{
  "assessment": "The source provides a minimal theoretical model of active droplets with two chemical reactions, showing a pitchfork bifurcation in droplet volume with fuel strength, excitability, and self-sustained oscillations. The key quantitative relations include the critical fuel strength for bistability (Eq. 12) and the cycle frequency scaling with k2 (Omega proportional to k2). The paper reports specific parameter values in Table 1 for figures, including fuel strength delta=4 (in units of k_BT) and k2/k1=1.0 for oscillation figures. The cycle frequency is stated to be weakly affected by delta, with a power-law dependence on k2. The source provides enough quantitative detail to support a numeric control (delta), a numeric readout (cycle frequency Omega), and a quantitative mechanism (Omega proportional to k2), but the exact numeric value of Omega is not given, only the scaling relation. Therefore, case_authoring_ready is set to false because no numeric readout value is reported; only a proportionality is stated.",
